3788:
Good news for you Adam, turning the power supply cor around does NOT make any difference. The way it is wired will work either way.
As for the reversed chip, when the unit didn't work, it was probably turned off fairly quickly. The old chips used a technology that would allow it to be in backwards for a short time. If it was left on for any long period, it would have overheated. We all know what THAT means!
Probably that resistor saved the chip. However, everyone I talked to about that fix said that you probably get erratic results because it is operating on too low of a power supply voltage. So removal is recommended.
Ken

