3794:
The fix that I am talking about is called "Krazy Koppen's Heat Sink" 

(Arcadian, Vol. 3, No. 8, Pg. 85 (June 8, 1981)):



http://www.ballyall ey.com/newslette rs/arcadian/ arcadian_ vol_3/arcadian_ vol_03_issue_ 08.pdf



I haven't taken a close look at the Astrocade with this fix, but I THINK 

that it is this one.  If it IS getting too little voltage, then why not just 

use a smaller resistor than the 30ohm resistor that is recommended?



Adam
OK, now I'm gonna get technical  on you!

When you put a resistor in a circuit, it develops a voltage drop across it as current goes through it. Current, which is what is causing the heat, will vary as the analog video stuff is being generated. The more the current, the more the voltage drop. The more the resistance, the more the voltage drop. Any drop can cause things to not work as designed. The Data chip also has a 2,5v output to the Modulator. As your current is fluctuates, so will this voltage, as well as several outputs. If by chance your unit is close to being marginal, these changes may cause undesirable outcomes.
Enough babbling, you get the picture.
Ken
