            I was going to work on my cartridge port on my Astrocade because if I'd bump 

the console at all it would reset.  Well, the fixed Astrocade doesn't have 

that problem.  I've really given it the test by trying my multicart and 

choosing games that require the multicart to be swapped out with AstroBASIC. 

  It works each time.  I would still like to fix the other Astrocade's 

cartridge port (or whatever is causing the problem), but now I have little 

incentive to do so.


**3 things to try here. 

1) Remove the top plastic from the Arcade and tahe a pencil eraser (the bar type works best here) and clean off the contacts of the cartridge slot.
2) If that still doesn't do it, then try CAREFULLY prying each pin up. This will give better contact to the pins. Be carefull not to bend them too much, because then the cart will not go in.
3)  You can take your carts apart and clead the contacts with the same eraser.
If none of these works, you may have a bad connection to something on the board. That requires a technician to troubleshoot and repair. $$$$$***
Ken

